<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Leuthen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1757</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Leuthen was fought on 5 December 1757 west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wroclaw">Breslau</a> in Silesia during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a> used the oblique order of attack to rout an Austrian army about twice the size of his own under Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-duke-of-lower-lorraine">Charles of Lorraine</a>. Coming a month after Rossbach, the victory restored Prussian control of Silesia and is often counted Frederick's masterpiece.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-leuthen.jpg" alt="Battle of Leuthen" width="320" height="255" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carl Röchling · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Leuthen_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
